cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (12.855-Octave, 0.0905-670.69 um) Space-Lyman to Herschel Submm/THz, HST STIS E140H, SOFIA EXES, JWST, Coherent Jerk-Drift, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space Lyman-limit/FUV/NUV (FUSE 0.0905-0.1187 um, HST/COS G130M
  0.1125-0.1450 um, HST/STIS E140H R=114,000 FUV, HST/STIS E140M 0.1145-0.1710 um,
  HST/STIS E230M/E230H 0.1605-0.3150 um), ground near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV), optical (HARPS,
  HARPS-N, ESPRESSO HR/UHR, Gemini GHOST BLUE+RED with simultaneous sky-IFU veto, Gemini
  GRACES, Euler CORALIE, OHP SOPHIE, OHP ELODIE, CFHT ESPaDOnS, MPG/ESO FEROS, VLT
  FLAMES/GIRAFFE HR), far-red (VLT UVES_RED, CARMENES_VIS with SERVAL RV alignment), 3-arm
  simultaneous UVB+VIS+NIR (VLT X-shooter 0.2989-2.4790 um), near-infrared YJH (NIRPS_HE),
  thermal J/H/K (VLT CRIRES+), SDSS APOGEE-2 H-band (up to N=28 visits), simultaneous YJHK
  (CFHT SPIRou APERO 0.7.295), JWST space optical-to-thermal-IR (NIRISS SOSS, NIRSpec
  G140H/G235H/G395H, MIRI LRS/MRS), airborne mid-IR echelon-echelle (SOFIA EXES
  5.62-26.13 um, R~86,000), Spitzer IRS SL+LL (5.20-37.86356 um), and Herschel far-IR/THz
  (PACS 51-210 um, SPIRE FTS 194-670.69 um, HIFI 0.56-1.16 THz at R=2.2e6) laser,
  cubic-jerk/periodic coherent shift-stack drift (DRIFT_V55 across 25 N>=4 campaigns /
  1.411B pixel integrals), greenhouse CCF, Dyson waste-heat vs. silicate-belt discrimination,
  and periodic frequency-comb technosignatures (0.0905-670.69081 um, 12.855 unbroken
  octaves across 30 spectrographs / 42 arms; 448 unique stars and 2,601 archival exposures
  totaling 772.806 h across V3.0-V5.5 + COMB_V4_1 with Keplerian planetary de-Doppler
  across 140 orbital campaigns, 39,942 synthetic calibration trials, 317,805 Legacy V2 false
  alarms eliminated, deterministic Stage-2 physical triage, and uniform all-sky COMB_V4_1
  filtering across 453 stacks), unified with 1.4 GHz Parkes/GBT radio searches and TESS
  photometry achieving 23/23 (100%) radio-echelle closure across a 448-system synthesis
  (0 verified ETI detections; 0.0973 W HST_STIS Proxima Cen, 0.065460 kW HST_STIS_E140H
  Alpha Cen A, 0.039712 kW JWST_NIRISS_SOSS SIMP 0136, 0.249612 kW ESO_FEROS GJ 1005,
  70.703128 kW HERSCHEL_SPIRE_FTS AB Aur, 235,044.17 kW HERSCHEL_HIFI R Dor, 58 calibrated
  panchromatic bridges across 728 cells [60 multi-phase targets] alongside 169 <10 pc
  stars with 1.4627 kW median limit).
